{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1377478-2e-non-sorcery-vampiric-magic","id":1377478,"title":"[2E] Non-Sorcery vampiric magic?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-31T01:51:27-07:00","id":1377478,"title":"[2E] Non-Sorcery vampiric magic?","content":"Is there a way to make non-magical Covenants to have appropriate magic ( Sorcery ) in theme? In <i>Castlevania</i> TV series Season 3 Invictus-like vampires makes magical rings that change your Oath of Loyalty in to slave making items. Is there a way for making something like that in <b>VtR</b> on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T03:47:01-07:00","id":1377485,"title":"","content":"Technically neither is non-magical because they all have magical advantages. If you want them all to have Blood Sorcery, then you could just replace their usual advantages with any of the various uncommon types of Blood Sorcery to the non-sorcerous Covenants as you see fit. Not that I would recommend it. The Circle and the Spear has Blood Sorcery because they're mystically and ritually inclined. Ordo Dracul instead have their Mysteries, Invictus their Oaths, and Carthians their Laws, because those are much more thematic for those Covenants. Blood Sorcery is also quite underwhelming in second edition because it takes way too long to set up for effects that often have a time limit.<br /> <br /> If it's just because you want some sort of magical edge to all of them, you're probably better off using Covenant specific Bloodlines with special Bloodline Disciplines to represent the mystical parts of Invictus and Carthians, or use of Devotions that are mostly confined to members of specific Covenants.<br /> Ordo Dracul already has mysticism and magic as part of their Mysteries, especially in their Scales, so no need to add anything to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T05:02:28-07:00","id":1377496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1377478-2e-non-sorcery-vampiric-magic?p=1377485#post1377485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically neither is non-magical because they all have magical advantages. If you want them all to have Blood Sorcery, then you could just replace their usual advantages with any of the various uncommon types of Blood Sorcery to the non-sorcerous Covenants as you see fit. Not that I would recommend it. The Circle and the Spear has Blood Sorcery because they're mystically and ritually inclined. Ordo Dracul instead have their Mysteries, Invictus their Oaths, and Carthians their Laws, because those are much more thematic for those Covenants. Blood Sorcery is also quite underwhelming in second edition because it takes way too long to set up for effects that often have a time limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only that the Rings I was having in mind looks <i>totally</i> as Oaths effect - only it's limited to enforcing it by the items. Are not the way for Oaths or Laws to be spread by the items they are put on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T05:22:32-07:00","id":1377498,"title":"","content":"Not without homebrew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-31T06:13:49-07:00","id":1377504,"title":"","content":"So you specifically ask if Vampire has a &quot;magic item creation&quot; rules? Because if so, then as Tessie said, it is an homebrew territory, but not that difficult homebrew territory. I mean, you could just reskin the Oaths of the Invictus to work through items instead of contracts. It is barely even an hack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T16:43:16-07:00","id":1379095,"title":"","content":"Mystery Cults can have abilities that are supernatural so yes but for what was done in Castlevania I would say it\u2019s an Invictus oath with a few modifications. The crafting rules exist in the CofD core mixed with the social combat rules and you can pull off something neatly exactly like what happened in the show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T21:44:51-07:00","id":1379174,"title":"","content":"I can get correctly that I can simply state: <i>'You can make any of your vampire powers trasmited by the Blood'</i> - and just <b>soak items with Blood</b> to have them like magical powers? And yes, probably would work then like crafting rules from<b> CoD Rulebook</b>?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T21:55:58-07:00","id":1379176,"title":"","content":"Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners has a write-up for Solomon Birch where he has an artifact called the 'Golden Mask.' He's wearing or holding it it in his art in the second edition core. It grants some powers specifically vampire-related and could be used as a guide for making similar objects but like everyone's saying it's just a matter of homebrew, and 'Give it Vitae, and it does this' is a really simple way to manage it. Though you can obviously get more complicated mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}